  "strategy": "We propose a genetic algorithm (GA) approach combined with local optimization to find a better solution for the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem. The GA will explore the search space for optimal step function configurations, while local optimization will refine promising candidates. This hybrid approach is designed to escape local optima and discover new solutions.\n\nKey improvements over the previous approach:\n- EAsearch for optimal h(x) configurations using a population-based method\n- Including multiple resolutions (n_points configurations) in the search\n- Using FFT-based correlation for faster performance\n- Local refinement with Adam optimization to escape local optima\n- Better handling of constraints through projection\n\nImplementation Procedure:\n1. Objective Function:\n   max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx is approximated using linear correlation:\n   max_k {correlation_result[k]} * (2.0/n_points)\n\n2. GA Implementation:\n   GA population with real-valued individuals in [0,1] satisfying sum=1\n   Fitness proportional to -C5 (lower C5 values are better)\n   Tournament selection with elitism\n   Simulated binary crossover (SBX) and polynomial mutation\n   After each generation, refine best individual with Adam optimization\n\n3. Candidate Handling:\n   All candidates satisfy 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and \u03a3h[i]=target_sum\n   Enforcement via projection after crossover/mutation\n\n4. Local Optimization:\n   Adam optimization with decaying learning rate\n   Gradient estimation using top-k contributions from correlation peaks\n\n5. Resolution Handling:\n   Maintain multiple resolutions (n_points)\n   Transfer best solution from one resolution to others\n\n6. Constraints Handling:\n   Project_sum function ensures h[i]\u2208[0,1] and \u03a3h[i]=target_sum\n   Without reconstruction: initial interpolation + projection\n\n7. Search Parameters:\n   Population size: 50\n   Generations: 50 initially, but time-based\n   Crossover rate: 0.8\n   Mutation rate: 0.2\n   eta_crossover and eta_mutation parameters for GA operators\n   Adam parameters: learning rates, moment parameters, cooldown steps\n\n8. Time Budget Management:\n   Time-based stopping\n   Early termination if no improvement\n   Timeout monitoring during optimization\n\n9. Validation and Output:\n   Return best solution and C5 value\n   Check constraints and ensure finite C5 value\n\nSearch Choices:\n- GA parameters: eta_crossover=20, eta_mutation=20, crossover_rate=0.8, mutation_rate=0.2\n- Adam parameters: initial LR=0.005, decay=0.99, starting batch size=16\n- Resolution sequence: [380, 460, 550, 680] (parent's resolution first)\n- Mutation: Polynomial mutation with bounds preservation\n- Selection: Tournament selection with elite count=5\n\nCompute Budget:\nResolution 380: ~100s\nResolution 460: ~90s\nResolution 550: ~70s\nResolution 680: ~50s\nTotal ~310s < 1100s budget\n\nValidation Contract:\n- Check optimization time remaining\n- Compute C5 using FFT-based correlation\n- Project and clip to satisfy constraints\n- Return (-log10(C5)) as score if C5 improves",
